<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">3 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 3 August, from 8 to 1981.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tiberius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">8 CE <span class="tih-ago">2,018 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tiberius defeats the Pannonian rebels at the River Bathinus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Roman forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a> defeated the rebel Breuci at the River Bathinus, and their leader Bato surrendered. It was a turning point in the great Illyrian revolt against Roman rule.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">881 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,145 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis III of West Francia defeats the Vikings at Saucourt</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King Louis III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-francia">West Francia</a> and his brother Carloman II defeated a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> army at Saucourt-en-Vimeu. The victory was celebrated in the Ludwigslied, an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-high-german">Old High German</a> poem of 59 rhyming couplets.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">908 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,118 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hungarian invaders defeat an East Frankish army at Eisenach</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An invading Hungarian army won a crushing victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eisenach">Eisenach</a> over an East Frankish army of troops from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>, led by Duke Burchard of Thuringia. The Hungarians had established their principality in the Carpathian Basin around 895.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-francia">East Francia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1347">1347 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">679 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Calais surrenders to Edward III after an eleven-month siege</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The French town of Calais capitulated to the English army of King Edward III, which had besieged it since September 1346. The surrender concluded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-crecy">Crécy</a> campaign, a series of large-scale raids across northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1492">1492 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">534 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Columbus sets sail from Palos on his first voyage</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a> left Palos de la Frontera with the Niña, Pinta and Santa María, seeking a westward route to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>. Ten weeks later he reached the Bahamas.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1778">1778 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">248 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">La Scala opera house opens in Milan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-scala">Teatro alla Scala</a> opened with Salieri's opera L'Europa riconosciuta. It became one of the world's leading opera houses, closely linked with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-verdi">Verdi</a>, Puccini and Toscanini.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1914">1914 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">112 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany declares war on France</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> declared war on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and prepared to strike through neutral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schlieffen-plan">Schlieffen Plan</a>. The invasion of Belgium the next day brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> into the war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schlieffen-plan">Schlieffen Plan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1936">1936 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">90 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jesse Owens wins the 100 metres at the Berlin Olympics</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Jesse Owens won the 100 metres, the first of four gold medals at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> Games. The success of a Black American athlete undercut Nazi propaganda about racial superiority.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1981">1981 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">45 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US air traffic controllers go on strike</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Nearly 13,000 members of the PATCO union walked out. President Reagan gave them 48 hours to return; he then fired more than 11,000, a defining moment for American labour relations.</p></div></li></ol>
